    "created_at": "2021-12-16T09:28:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-16T09:38:05Z",
    "body": "This is not a bug. The processing of `data:` URLs is specified by the fetch spec (https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#data-urls), and `#` in URL syntax is a fragment marker. URL fragments are not sent to the server, or used in fetching at all, so it makes sense that they're also skipped when decoding `data:` URLs.\r\n\r\nIf you want to use arbitrary characters in `data:` URLs, you have to [percent-encode them](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#percent-encoded-bytes) (for example, with `encodeURIComponent(data)` in Javascript).",
